From a16eefd1f6ec4f509a0a62b9b4165a9892d28e4e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Samuel Price <thesamprice@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 15 Nov 2026 01:30:36 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 9/9] opcodes: microblaze: symbolize addresses at or above
 0x80000000

print_insn_microblaze computes the target of a branch or the address
in an immediate as an int, tests it with "immval > 0" and passes it to
symbol_at_address_func sign-extended to bfd_vma.  An address at or
above 0x80000000, where many boards put their memory, is negative, so
objdump names no symbol: linked at 0x90000000,

	brlid	r15, 20
	addik	r3, r0, 32
	bri	-20		// 90000000

where at 0x10000000 the same code shows <far>, <dat> and <_start>.

Compute the address as a 32-bit bfd_vma.  Keep skipping address 0,
which the "> 0" tests also did, so that output for objects is
unchanged.  Four ld tests expected the raw addresses for code linked at
0x90000000; they now show the symbols.

opcodes/
	* microblaze-dis.c (get_imm_value): New function.
	(print_insn_microblaze): Use it, and compute addresses as
	32-bit bfd_vma.

ld/
	* testsuite/ld-microblaze/disas-high.d: New test.
	* testsuite/ld-microblaze/disas-high.s: New file.
	* testsuite/ld-microblaze/relax-64-none.d: Expect symbols for
	addresses above 0x80000000.
	* testsuite/ld-microblaze/relax-addend.d: Likewise.
	* testsuite/ld-microblaze/relax-no-keep-memory.d: Likewise.
	* testsuite/ld-microblaze/relax-wrap.d: Likewise.
	* testsuite/ld-microblaze/relax-align.d: Likewise.

Assisted-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
